It could just have been a chameleon that was at some point polymorphed 
into a creature (such as a gnome) that picked up a bow, then never 
polymorphed into a creature (such as a lichen) that was forced to drop 
it until just then. There's also a possibility that the chameleon was 
generated with the bow - I'm not sure how initial inventory generation 
is handled for them.

Alternatively, it could have been a poly trap, and the demon 
accidentally triggered the trap again. As I read the code, this would 
not have produced any additional messages - only deliberate monster use 
produces messages (e.g. "The kobold deliberately jumps onto a polymorph 
trap!")

